		("UI-101", "the park camera's field of view is 55 degrees where tp.exe's projection has 90: the camera init 0x42A990 hands pi/2 (scaled by 180/pi, 0x6fdd80) and the first-frame setup 0x54E86F hands 90.0 to the projection builder 0x578BE0 (near 0.1, far 1000), which multiplies degrees by pi/180 and halves them and scales x and y alike by cos of that half angle over sin (the builder reads no aspect, so 90 is the angle of both axes before the viewport maps the clip square to the window), and 0x56b790 takes the same 90.0 for the picking frustum (half extents 0.5 and 0.5 / the aspect word 0x8bcbcc); the park view's default pose after the Home reset in 0x42b1c0 is the target (475, 0, 175) (cell (47, 17), ten units a cell) at height 110 with yaw 0; OpenTPW's park camera pose (height, pull-back, yaw) is its own and was tuned to 55 (the free-walk and ride cameras also use 55)", "how 0x42b1c0 turns target, height and yaw into the eye position and pitch (its eye computation after the pan code), whether the camera zoom and view buttons change the field of view, and the aspect word 0x8bcbcc (written outside the code's direct stores), then a capture of the original park view to fit OpenTPW's pose to it"),
